WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.864
You get skinny and then you want to cover it up.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:12.032
I just wore clothing, baggy clothes, things that hid my body.

00:00:14.336 --> 00:00:17.360
I would have little games in my head that I would play

00:00:18.616 --> 00:00:20.736
like let's see how long I can go without eating.

00:00:22.016 --> 00:00:27.136
I would definitely still be starving myself if I had not found circus artists.

00:00:35.584 --> 00:00:38.400
I’m Kayla Dyches and I’m a professional aerialist

00:00:38.656 --> 00:00:40.192
and a survivor of anorexia.

00:00:41.472 --> 00:00:47.360
I did gymnastics and developed anorexia in my teens into my 20s.

00:00:47.616 --> 00:00:50.176
At my lowest point I was 90 pounds,

00:00:50.432 --> 00:00:52.480
and that's when I discovered circus arts.

00:00:53.248 --> 00:00:56.192
It changed my life because I knew 

00:00:56.648 --> 00:00:59.392
that if I wanted to do it, I needed to grow stronger

00:01:00.672 --> 00:01:02.208
and grow from it.

00:01:05.792 --> 00:01:10.236
It took me 8 years to get from there to here.

00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:13.240
Anorexia never really goes away,

00:01:14.152 --> 00:01:17.000
you just learn how to shut it out.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:24.480
When I look in the mirror now, I don't see the muscle mass. I feel small.

00:01:24.736 --> 00:01:28.280
Almost immediately I’m thinking, “you know that's not true.”

00:01:28.632 --> 00:01:31.864
“You can climb two hundred feet straight up.” 

00:01:35.132 --> 00:01:40.192
I had no idea from my first day that this would end up being my profession.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.776
Back then, you know, I would cook

00:01:48.032 --> 00:01:49.312
a pot of noodles

00:01:49.824 --> 00:01:52.896
And I would have to get my then-husband

00:01:53.176 --> 00:01:57.320
to strain the noodles for me because I didn't have the strength 

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.320
to lift the pot of water and noodles and pour it out.

00:02:01.344 --> 00:02:04.416
I remember asking, “what is wrong with me?”

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.768
And one of my trainers looked at me and she said, “You need to eat.”

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.192
I had fallen in love with aerial so much so that I was willing to put food in my mouth

00:02:16.704 --> 00:02:22.080
and grow some muscle so I can get up in the air and keep up with all my classmates.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.128
If I could say anything to my anorexic self,

00:02:33.784 --> 00:02:36.928
it would be that “you could be so much nicer to your body.”

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.976
At the time, I thought I was taking care of it.

00:02:39.232 --> 00:02:43.072
I wasn’t, and I didn't know any better.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.936
I'm capable of so much more.

